# Parsers

- Register provider parsers in `parsers/bootstrap.py` **before** `GenericHeuristicParser`
- Prefer provider YAML in `config/providers/` for discovery; put hard classification logic in Python parsers
- Axis salary: `SALARY_REF` matching `NEFT|IMPS|RTGS/.../Sala(ry)?`
- Non-salary Axis credits → transfer/refund + `needs_review` / `excludes_from_spending` as appropriate — never auto-income
- Axis declined card alerts (`Transaction declined…`) → `not_a_transaction`, exclude from spending/review
- Scapia Federal card alerts are **debits** (purchases). Never treat “Credit Card” wording as money-in. Parser: `parsers/scapia.py`
- Direction heuristics must not use bare `\bcredit\b` / `\bdebit\b` (card-type false positives)
- Amount regexes must accept leading decimals (`INR .52`)
- Include `UPILITE` alongside UPI/NEFT/IMPS/RTGS channel tokens
- Enrichment fields go through `classification/enrichment.py` via pipeline persist
- Backfill: `python -m expense_tracker.reclassify_axis` or `python -m expense_tracker.reclassify_scapia` with `force_reparse`
